### Step 1 Continuity and Context Stability

Step 1 serves as the procedural bridge confirming session continuity between turn instantiation and requirement decomposition. It guarantees that the execution context has not suffered memory corruption, nonce substitution, or context drift. Step 1 re-verifies that ChatGPT maintains ownership of the execution sequence while asserting identical `nonce`, `run_nonce`, and `user_request` attributes.

During supervisory evaluation, Gemini compares the `step_1_record` against the persisted `start_of_turn` artifact stored in `state.json`. Any divergence in textual content or identifier attributes indicates an integrity failure, halting the pipeline. Step 1 ensures that downstream requirement extraction in Step 2 operates upon an uncorrupted, verified baseline.

