### Step 3 Decomposition, Modifier Recursion, and Test Batteries

Step 3 represents the core planning engine. It deconstructs the effective instruction set into discrete semantic clauses (Section B), analyzes all modifying clauses recursively (Section C), synthesizes a strictly aligned execution plan P (Section D), projects conditional UI output (Section E), and subjects the plan to an automated 31-question test battery (Section F).

The test suite is imported from the canonical artifact specified in `config.json` under `step3_evaluation_artifact`. Each test represents a known operational vulnerability, such as unverified assumptions, path divergence, or unstated additions. In Step 3.G, loop control evaluates the test battery: if any test yields `T` (True, indicating a failure condition), the state machine executes an internal repeat, resetting planning from Section A. Only when all 31 tests return `F` (False, indicating zero defects) can `Loop_Decision` become `"False"` and `return_schema_completed` be marked `true`.

