The integration contract between `Agents.md` and `send-to-gemini.js` establishes an immutable, self-verifying state machine. The system rejects any architecture where supervisory validation relies upon model introspection or generated self-assessments. In this dual-model framework, ChatGPT provides generative planning and execution, while Gemini functions as an incorruptible supervisory authority bound by physical runtime evidence.

Deterministic evidence collection occurs outside the model context. Prior to invoking the supervisory evaluator, the NodeJS runtime scans filesystem paths, examines git object storage, queries process execution tables, and injects immutable ground-truth findings into the prompt. Gemini is required to evaluate these findings structurally within `ground_truth_verification_eval`. If the runtime discovers that a claimed commit does not exist, or that an edited file lacks the asserted content, that finding is flagged as blocking. The supervisory gate cannot issue a PASS over a blocking finding, eliminating false positives and preventing execution hallucinations.

